+### OI-48: A moved branch manager keeps the old branch for up to 15 minutes
+
+- **Where:** §17.2 Business Logic, Branch assignments (chunk 13b)
+- **Type:** Inconsistency
+- **Concern:** The `branch-assignment-refresh` job reads API-06 every 15 minutes, and a sign-in session reads it for its branch manager only at the first branch request, so a branch manager moved to another branch during a session keeps the old branch's requests for up to 15 minutes. A removed staff role ends within 5 minutes (§16.8, through the 5-minute access token of chunk 06). Two staff changes that end access to a branch's requests take effect in different bounds.
+- **Options:**
+  - **A.** Read API-06 every 5 minutes - a moved branch manager loses the old branch within the bound of a removed role; three times the scheduled API-06 reads.
+  - **B.** Keep 15 minutes and state the longer bound in §16.8 - no added load; two bounds for staff changes stay.
+  - **C.** Read API-06 at every branch request - no stale window; every branch page then depends on the Retail IT system answering.
+- **Recommended Answer:** Option A - §17.2 Business Logic, Branch assignments: "the `branch-assignment-refresh` job reads API-06 every 15 minutes" becomes "the `branch-assignment-refresh` job reads API-06 every 5 minutes".
+- **Why:** A removed role and a moved branch manager are both staff changes that end access to a branch's requests; option A gives them one bound, while B keeps a documented 15-minute window on the old branch and C ties every branch page to an outside system. No option adds business behaviour. The tradeoff accepted: three times the scheduled API-06 reads.
+- **Status:** Decided - pending application: Option A, decided by the test PM on 2026-10-07; the next request applies it.
+
+---
